<article class="env-lemma" id="0AP7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AP7">Lemma <span data-tag="0AP7">37.66.6</span>.</a> The property of being ind-quasi-affine is stable under base change. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $f : X \to Y$ be an ind-quasi-affine morphism. For checking that every base change of $f$ is ind-quasi-affine, by Lemma <a href="/tag/0F1U" data-tag="0F1U">37.66.2</a>, we may work Zariski locally on $Y$, so we assume that $Y$ is affine. Furthermore, we may also assume that in the base change morphism $Z \to Y$ the scheme $Z$ is affine, too. The base change $X \times _ Y Z \to X$ is an affine morphism, so, by Lemmas <a href="/tag/0F1V" data-tag="0F1V">37.66.3</a> and <a href="/tag/0F1W" data-tag="0F1W">37.66.4</a>, the map $X \times _ Y Z \to Y$ is ind-quasi-affine. Then, by Lemma <a href="/tag/0F1X" data-tag="0F1X">37.66.5</a>, the base change $X \times _ Y Z \to Z$ is ind-quasi-affine, as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>